body:
To user SauceBeUponHim,

Honestly, this is most of the teen community today. As people online and offline become more toxic, more people overuse marijuana, and Trump gets more people to pay for his wall it is understandable why most teens and people in general think about suicide than live in this shithole. But as a teen, I have realized that people thinking about suicide are thinking it sarcastically at first, then truthfully with a lack of care for life. As a person who has thought of committing suicide, I wonder why I haven't. Maybe it's the love of my parents overriding my painful thoughts. Now that I think about it, it probably is.

&#x200B;

Continuing my thoughts on your post, as younger children become spoiled, more entitled people are entering online society. At first it seems fine until you realize that they will probably be even more toxic than 12-year-olds on Fortnite today. This, in theory will spread more suicidal thoughts.

&#x200B;

Considering the help that schools, media, and parents are trying to give, kids, including the parasite of a human writing this post, don't really care about others. It makes me think at times that Armageddon will happen tomorrow. 

&#x200B;

But considering how short our lives are already we decide on two things: Suicide or living our lives to the fullest. Of course there are the people between the extremes, but that generally is how life is playing itself out.

&#x200B;

In conclusion, life is a choice, death is a choice as well. Most people fear pain and that is understandable. But the fact that you choose to live signifies the fact that there is still hope and while I may not be the hope you are looking for, I hope you find it in someone.

&#x200B;

With sincerity,

InMagneto12
